<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28277" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mĕābĭlis</span></b> ,
		e, adj.
		meo. * <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Pass., passable, that can be passed through</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">transitus vel bubus meabilis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin. 6,
					1, 1, § 2</span></i>
			.— * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Act., passing through, penetrating</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aër per cuncta rerum meabilis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					2, 5, 4, § 10</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
